WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.256 --> 00:00:02.937
- [Narrator] In the '80s when
lots of people were playing

00:00:02.937 --> 00:00:06.931
arcade games like Pac Man,
Donkey Kong and Frogger,

00:00:06.931 --> 00:00:09.954
this is what they were
playing in Soviet Russia.

00:00:09.954 --> 00:00:12.537
(game beeping)

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:31.855
- [Narrator] That's Alexander,
he runs the Museum of Soviet

00:00:31.855 --> 00:00:35.272
Arcade Machines in St. Petersburg Russia.

00:00:57.854 --> 00:00:59.731
- [Narrator] Unlike their
western counterparts,

00:00:59.731 --> 00:01:02.314
the games weren't just for fun.

00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:19.408
- [Narrator] The point of the
games was training for the

00:01:19.408 --> 00:01:22.288
Soviet Army, building
skills like reasoning,

00:01:22.288 --> 00:01:25.538
hand-eye coordination and marksmanship.

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:49.608
- [Narrator] All the Soviet
arcade games were built in

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:53.034
military factories using
leftover parts from weapons,

00:01:53.034 --> 00:01:56.617
refrigerators, calculators
and other items.

00:02:07.553 --> 00:02:09.343
- [Narrator] But now,
decades after the fall

00:02:09.343 --> 00:02:11.010
of the Soviet Union.

00:02:20.176 --> 00:02:22.843
(upbeat music)

